  "problem": "The slope of the tangent to the curve at $A$ is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "We use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x$ for $x\\le 1.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(0).$ In part 5, we found that\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)={e}^{x}+2x+1,\\,x<1.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(0) & ={e}^{0}+2(0)+1 \\\\  & =1+0+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $2.$",
